{"ld": 1022, "paper": "SP440", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Protect and Increase Access to Justice in Civil Legal Matters for Persons with Low Incomes (EMERGENCY)", "sponsor_id": "s-carney-anne", "cosponsor_ids": ["s-bennett-richard", "h-dhalac-deqa", "h-kuhn-amy", "h-moonen-matthew", "s-moore-marianne", "h-poirier-jennifer", "h-rana-ambureen", "s-rotundo-margaret"], "committee_code": "JUD", "committee_name": "Judiciary", "summary": {"text": "This bill provides for increases in the ongoing appropriation to the Judicial Department for civil legal services. The appropriation supplements existing revenue from ongoing sources and replaces one-time funding with additional ongoing revenue to be distributed to providers of civil legal services by determination of the Maine Civil Legal Services Fund Commission. The bill also provides an ongoing minimum amount to be appropriated annually to the Maine Civil Legal Services Fund. It requires the joint standing committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over judiciary matters to hold a public hearing on civil legal services funding in 2026 and biennially thereafter and to make a recommendation to the Governor and the Legislature based on those hearings regarding additional funding for civil legal services. The bill also requires an annual report by the commission to the joint standing committee of the Legislature having jurisdiction over 1503 judiciary matters.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0440&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "died", "status_label": "Died On Adjournment", "final_disposition": {"label": "Died On Adjournment", "date": "2026-04-29", "governor_action": null, "governor_action_date": null}, "fiscal_status": "Fiscal Impact", "fiscal_note_url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/bills_132nd/fiscalpdfs/FN102201.pdf", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 1022)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper